WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.860
Salt Fish

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.360
I had no idea such power really existed.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.610
Just do your best to keep it safe.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.410
Until I get there, that is.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.360
Huh?

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.870
It's the great Galileo's inheritance.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.370
It's only proper that I should retrieve it myself.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.540
You're taking it right away?

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.130
What about the sketches?

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.570
What about the remaining half—

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.260
I can't stop him anymore.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.120
Those girls will be killed.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.270
Kazuki

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.270
For sure.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.450
Ow!

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:09.630
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:09.630
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:17.430
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:17.430
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:24.680
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:24.680
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.770
shinkuromanika

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.770
Synchromanica

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.310
itsu no ma ni ka

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.310
Before I know it

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.480
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.480
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:37.780
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:37.780
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:44.290
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:44.290
I can hear someone's dream

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:51.250
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:51.250
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.060
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.060
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.390
shinkuromanika

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.390
Synchromanica

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.520
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.520
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.570
shinkuromanika

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.570
Synchromanica

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.780
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.780
The synchrony of your life

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:29.210
The Caspi stretches on for so very long!

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:36.370
So much salt; it's extremely salty!

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.630
Thanks for the food!

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.180
Looks yummy.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.010
Good job, Kakkii!

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.520
Isn't this usually <i>your</i> job, Haa-nee?

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.260
Sylvia

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:58.030
Hozuki

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.930
But I'm still recovering.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.390
Then if you weren't, you would've cooked?

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.440
This is delicious!

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.680
You're ignoring me?

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.030
Yum!

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.530
R-Really?

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:03.490
Yeah, I haven't had curry this good for ages.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.660
But it's supposed to be beef stew...

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.710
Well, it is hard to mess up curry.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.290
I just said it's supposed to be beef stew!

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.460
You said that on purpose, didn't you?

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.420
Where have you been?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.590
You shouldn't ask a lady that.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.420
Oh, you were pooping?

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.120
Idiot, we're eating!

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.260
It's nice and smooth.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.850
Don't be vulgar!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.480
It isn't like Anna-san did it right here.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.640
Stop making a big deal out of it, Kakkii.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:37.170
Hocchii was bringing me up to speed.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.190
Oh.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:44.200
That warm light that saved us...

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.830
I think that light

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.330
was some kind of powerful energy.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.330
I can't believe what happened.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:57.090
It got warm in an instant, and the blizzard died down, too...

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.440
It only makes sense if we assume that what we saw was some new type of energy.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.340
But nobody would really care about this, right?

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:08.850
That's why we came up with a kind of theory.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:12.810
Right now, Adnimoon is hot on our heels.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:16.520
They want the Galileo Tesoro,
despite the fact that we have no idea know what it is.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.610
Right.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.230
Anyway, Adnimoon Company

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.880
is a globally famous energy-development corporation.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.770
What is it that they'd want...

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:30.850
What they'd be willing to kill for right now...

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.870
It's pretty obvious, isn't it?

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.750
Energy resources.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.380
Yeah.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.920
That's probably correct.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:43.610
Then maybe this Galileo Tesoro they're after is some kind of energy resource.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.760
And, Anhedo-san...

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:49.850
You knew that, didn't you?

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:57.400
But I had no idea that hourglass had such power...

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.730
So you don't deny that you've known what the Tesoro was.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.280
Is that the truth, Anna-san?

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.450
Well done.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.870
Why?

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.760
Why didn't you tell us what the Tesoro really was?!

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.500
I thought you'd lose your nerve if I did.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:20.330
You three are the only ones who can find the energy source that might save this world.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:23.140
Are you really capable of bearing that burden?

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.010
Save the world...

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:29.010
Do you really have the resolve to bear the hopes

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.520
of the entire world?

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.510
Of course not...

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.040
Don't underestimate us!

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:40.150
I'm trying to become an adjudicator of the law.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.320
I'm totally primed to bear a hope that will crush great evil!

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.770
The world is too big a place for me to imagine.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.450
But...

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.200
I believe we can't keep on this way!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.290
If there is something I can do, I want to do it!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.290
Well said, Hocchii!

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.040
I did underestimate you all.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.540
You aren't Galileo Galilei's descendants for nothing.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.100
That has nothing to do with this.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.850
In any case...

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.180
What do you think that is?

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.140
Huh?

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.260
Well,

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.810
why do you have that anyway, Hocchii?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.430
Oh, um...

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.810
I found it in the attic with the sketch.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.060
I just thought it was pretty.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.980
Then you had no idea that it was anything important?

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.150
And what do we plan to do with it?

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.740
If the Tesoro is energy,

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:34.580
couldn't that hourglass be the Tesoro itself?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:40.040
If we hang on to that, won't the bad guys keep coming after us?

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.580
Indeed.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.210
Naturally, we have no intention of surrendering it.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.420
Didn't think so.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:51.390
Adnimoon is monopolizing methane hydrate.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:57.160
If this hourglass's energy fell into their hands,
they'd never share it with the other companies!

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.060
You're right...

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.860
So we can't give it to them, of all people.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:06.800
The power to save the world should be used the right way, by the right people!

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.840
Anna-san?

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.400
You look like you've done something naughty.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.800
I might have lied.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:35.760
I get what Haa-nee's saying.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.190
The world needs to change.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:42.390
But I...

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.400
To be honest,

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.790
I might prefer to just finish collecting the sketches.

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.200
It's weird, right?

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:56.780
There shouldn't be anything more important than saving the world.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.660
That isn't necessarily true.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:07:59.790
Huh?

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:03.170
What matters most is different for everyone.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.830
What's most important?

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.920
What's worth fighting for?

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.760
It's okay if those are different for different people.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.440
Anna-san, what is it for you?

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.880
What's important and worth fighting for?

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:18.470
Love.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.520
Eh?!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:24.190
I could do anything for the one I love.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.520
Anything.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.410
Love?

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:28.860
Um...

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:34.610
Is it still too hard for you to understand what it means to be in love?

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.370
I... I know!

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:40.120
He saved me.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:42.700
No, that isn't right.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:47.380
By clinging to his strength, I was saved.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:52.920
He's never looked at me. Not once.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:56.240
But I also liked that kind of strength he had.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:09:00.630
As far as he's concerned, I may as well not exist.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.400
He has no need for me.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.730
Even so, I want to help him.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.650
That's how he makes me feel.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.850
Anna-san...

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:20.660
It's kind of nice...

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.730
It sounds so wonderful...

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:30.240
Love,

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:31.920
romance...

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.840
Liking...

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.130
It's strange...

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.680
Just from reading the words,

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.430
I can feel emotions so intense, they're almost painful.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:42.610
I hope that someday, I'll also...

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:45.350
Have your first kiss. "Smooch," ain't it?

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:49.100
Don't interrupt! Leave me alone!

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.210
Wait, why are you using a Kansai dialect?

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:55.360
Since you added it, I've been thinking of using it.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:57.610
Japanese is wonderful.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.110
I mean, it rocks.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.140
Doesn't it?

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:03.910
And language isn't the only great thing about Japan...

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.410
There are one-of-a-kind customs and old buildings,

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:10.680
not to mention unforgettable snacks and food...

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:13.210
They have a fun, unique culture.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.720
I especially love their kimonos.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:17.670
I'd like to wear one some day.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.810
I bet it'd look real cute.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:23.720
I'm definitely going to take the <i>Galileo</i> there someday!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.390
Well, lemme see...

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:30.400
What?

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:41.690
The enemy?

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:42.780
It looks that way.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.790
Oh, dear... Scary torpedoes!

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.170
Those hulks again?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.440
Are they after the hourglass?

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:14.770
That toy is too good for the likes of you.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:17.280
We'll have you relinquish it.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.280
Hocchii, they're coming head-on!

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.870
What're you going to do, Hocchii?!

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:32.960
Kaa-nee, Assault Mode!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:36.090
Wh-Why me? Whatever...

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.920
Goldfish, Assault Mode.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.260
She isn't "Goldfish"!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.650
Who cares about that right now?

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:45.260
My bad. Assault Mode's a bust!

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.600
Failure

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:47.640
The water pressure is too high down here.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:48.770
She can't transform.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.390
Then surface!

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.440
But isn't the enemy up above, waiting for us?

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.690
Isn't it better than staying here and losing our options?

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:55.690
Hurry!

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.320
We can't let these guys get the hourglass!

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.450
Changing to Assault Mode!

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.960
Here we go!

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.260
Here they come.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.680
Begin counterattack!

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:31.680
What?

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.690
What's this?

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.800
No way...

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:13.490
Soon, the Galileo Tesoro will be within my grasp.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:21.070
I have created the perfect son.

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.790
Don't you agree?

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.130
No!

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:46.850
Don't stop!

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:47.590
Keep it up!

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.640
I give up!

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:56.450
What about our weapons?

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:58.230
Don't we have any other weapons?

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:02.480
What's wrong?

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:04.650
Put up more of a fight.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.300
The boosters!

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:15.540
This is bad! This is bad!

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.250
We're done for...

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.780
Ow...

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.760
Are you okay, Hocchii? Kakkii?

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:02.600
We're completely surrounded.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.460
Doesn't look like we can break through.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.850
What should we do, Haa-nee?!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:11.750
We'll have to hope for a miracle.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:19.140
Oh?

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:22.650
Hey!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.980
Come down here,

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:26.100
rich boy!

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:29.610
You're saying a man like you can't handle women face-to-face?!

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:31.150
What a loser.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:33.690
And you call yourself a CEO's son?!

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.300
Hazuki-chan, stop...

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.710
He'll kill you!

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.960
Isn't this what you want?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.960
Then come and get it!

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.110
Come on!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.200
Haa-nee!

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:22.330
You thought you could make it out of here if you took me hostage?

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.370
What a rather naïve strategy.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:41.470
Just take it, already!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.230
Kaa-nee...

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.230
I don't want to deal with this anymore.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:47.780
Let's just end it.

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:49.480
You can have the stupid thing.

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:51.190
Just...

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.610
Just leave us alone!

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.620
That's enough, isn't it?

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.380
Please leave.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.360
Kaa-nee...

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.170
Kaa-nee?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.350
Um...

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:57.470
Listen—

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.720
For now, let her be.

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:03.470
Okay...

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:16.160
I couldn't do anything...

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:19.810
I didn't want to give it up, no matter what.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:23.390
I didn't want to lose to a guy like that.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:26.540
Why did it have to be this way?

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:27.730
Damn it!

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.730
Please don't blame Kazuki-chan.

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:32.710
If she hadn't done that, we'd all be—

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.180
I know!

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.960
You want to say we'd all be dead, right?!

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:40.290
Knowing that doesn't make it any easier.

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:43.010
It's over now...

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.430
Better to forget.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.440
How can we forget?

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:51.600
In the end, we lost to those with power. And they took everything!

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.700
We're going to continue our trip?

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.950
Wh-Why?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:15.420
If the Galileo Tesoro still waits for us at the end of these sketches,

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.550
we can still turn things around.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:21.810
We'll find the Tesoro and one-up them.

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:26.360
We'll never lose to them again!

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:30.550
We'll find the sketches ourselves...

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:35.730
Haa-nee and Hocchibi are such idiots.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:39.770
Why do we have to go so far?

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:41.040
Kazuki-chan...

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:44.030
I can't be responsible for the entire world.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:49.080
All I want is for everyone to be safe...

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.390
Take that,

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
you iron-masked bastard!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:15.060
Haa-nee, don't be so reckless!

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.900
This way was faster.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.230
Jeez...

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:19.320
Oh!

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.650
There it is!

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:23.490
There!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.450
Yeah!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.120
There it is, Haa-nee!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.370
Drying them indoors just doesn't work.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:36.660
They need the sun.

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:38.380
You're awfully chipper.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:41.460
We're still at a disadvantage.

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:45.390
We can't stay all gloom-and-doom forever.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.720
We have clean laundry

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.390
and we found hope.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.000
So we have to keep positive.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.230
Hope...

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:56.070
Right.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:58.930
Where to next?

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:02.610
Still analyzing. Just a sec!

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:08.170
Got it.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:10.200
Our next stop's here.

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:13.710
That's...

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:19.960
Japan!

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:41.150
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:41.150
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:44.990
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:44.990
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:51.990
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:51.990
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:57.120
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:57.120
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:01.500
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:01.500
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:06.800
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:06.800
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:14.770
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:14.770
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:23.150
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:23.150
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:30.280
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:30.280
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:42.420
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:42.420
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
